  "result": "The node didn't pass: the gate ends at `WITNESS_FAIL`, and the cause is in the node's own plan, not in the files. Its `blind` scenario can't be built, so I stopped and reported it in `task_result.md`. All other planned witnesses reach their verdicts, plus the two I added. I used 4 of the 6 gate runs.\n\n**Why `blind` can't be built:** the plan asks for both vehicles in lane L with `rel.longitudinal_overlap` unobserved. Masking that atom only removes a supplied measurement, and Core then recomputes the overlap from the two vehicles' footprints. A scene is only accepted if every vehicle whose lane occupancy is observed has a full footprint, and the rule needs both occupancies. So the overlap is always known when the scene is valid. When I withheld the car's extent to hide it, the gate rejected the trace. The plan should mask `ru.aggregate` instead, which blanks the vehicles' classes; I give an example scene in `task_result.md`.\n\n**The rule** (`NRS_486_351_2.lean`):\n- **Who it applies to:** the subject is a motorcycle, moped or trimobile (the node's three definitions).\n- **The duty:** for every other vehicle v and every lane L that both occupy with overlap ≥ 0, the pair must be excused.\n- **When the pair is excused:** both are motorcycles or mopeds, their headings are aligned (`rel.same_direction` with `p.side_by_side_same_direction_cos`), and at most two vehicles ride abreast in L.\n- **\"Two abreast\":** written as a count using the text's literal 2. Core has no count unit constructor, so I wrote it as `Units.ratio 2 1`. The gate stopped at the witnesses, so its literal and static checks haven't run on this yet.\n- **Narrowings:** none added.\n\n**Two other plan issues:**\n- **`forbid` (\"a motorcycle beside a car\") is unknown, not violated, if the car goes the same way.** The run's reading leaves the `motor_vehicle` class unresolved under the motorcycle and moped definitions, so the car can never be decided \"not a motorcycle or moped\". My `forbid` uses an oncoming car, so the heading check decides it. The reading or plan should look at whether `motor_vehicle` ought to stay unresolved there.\n- **`idle`'s \"passenger car\" subject is unknown for the same reason.** I used a bicycle instead, which is outside all three definitions.\n\n**Witnesses added:** `branch_4` (two mopeds side by side → compliant) and `branch_5` (two motorcycles abreast head-on → violated).\n\n**Mistakes on my side:** I re-ran the gate once without changing anything, which wasted a run. I also tried `gate --help`, which was denied and didn't run.",
